The definition of $\artanh{x}$ is 

$$
\artanh{x} = \dfrac{1}{2}\ln\left(\dfrac{1+x}{1-x}\right).
$$

Therefore,

$$
\eqalign{
\artanh\left ( \dfrac{1}{2} \right )

& = \dfrac{1}{2}\ln\left(\dfrac{1+\dfrac{1}{2}}{1-\dfrac{1}{2}}\right)\[5pt]

&=\dfrac{1}{2}\ln\left(\dfrac{\dfrac{3}{2}}{\dfrac{1}{2}}\right)\[5pt]

&=\dfrac{1}{2}\ln{3}.
}
$$

